Z||000000||stingant0||12-05-2001||03:36 PM||||I went back yesterday yo look at the engine again. It has 24,000 miles not 28,000. It came out of a 96 monte carlo. I had the guy through in wiring also. The problem is that I have to pull it out. The wiring is from a 95 monte carlo not a 96, will this work. Also how hard is it to pull the wiring out. In my fiero it wasn't very hard. Can I just disconnect the wiring from the fire wall? The guy also has a 3.4 dohc with a getrag he just got in, he wants $1000 for it. No computer though. I don't have the money to buy that engine and tranny but if anyone is interested I can find more out about it.<P>ps. how do I put pictures on here? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||12-05-2001||08:35 PM||||I'm just in the planning stages of this myself (other than having the motor). From what I've read so far, if you're going to run it with a 5 speed, I believe you want the use a 91-93 ECM. I'm thinking it would be easier to adapt 91-93 wiring to a 95/96 motor than vice-versa. Hopefully someone that's already done it will confirm or deny this??? <P>To post pics, click on the blue/red Pennock Image Poster icon at the bottom of most pages on here and follow the instructions.||||reg||1
