Z||000005||88-DOHC||12-05-2001||11:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stingant0:<BR><B>Joe he only has this monte carlo out there, but it still has an engine in it. My AOL IM is microwave1779 so IM me is you want to know anything more..I'm having second thoughts about doing this conversion. It just seems to complicated with making the motor mounts and all.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Making motor mounts? If you mount the 3.4 DOHC upto the Fiero stock tranny, it should bolt right up to the existing motor mounts. No modification needed. Again the hard part of this swap is the ECM and wiring. However if you plan on using the donor tranny, then mods may have to be done (I really don't know for sure). <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||stingant0||12-06-2001||12:24 AM||||maybe I misread something about making a motor mount? I only need the wiring to the computer from the donor car right?||||reg||1
Z||000007||88-DOHC||12-06-2001||03:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stingant0:<BR><B>maybe I misread something about making a motor mount? I only need the wiring to the computer from the donor car right?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Well, having only done this swap on an 88, I can't say for certain whether the 84-87 cradles would need modification. Perhaps they would, I dunno. Someone like West Coast Fiero's could answer that one for certian. I do know for the 88 cradle no mods were needed.<P>Yes, if your going to make your own wiring harness you will need the donor harness.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FormulaJoe||12-06-2001||08:34 AM||||Motor mounts are the same I believe.  Only things you have to make from scratch is an exhaust system (and not a total system unless you want to) and that is not a biggie.  After the exhaust the wiring is the other big hurdle.  Fuel, cooling and  intake are just a matter of hooking them up.  Sorry I dont do IM's,  dont have any software to do them.  And this is if you use the Fiero tranny.  As someone said in another post if you use the tranny from the donor car you need to modify mounts. Also you would need a neutral balanced flywheel for a manual conversion, I have an '88 so mine is.<P>------------------<BR>Yellow Formula<BR>(soon to be 3.4 DOHC)<p>[This message has been edited by FormulaJoe (edited 12-06-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000009||DKOV||12-06-2001||10:05 AM||||88s, at times, do need a minor subframe mod.  Apparently there are two slighlty different versions of the 88 frame...  The only variance is that, on the passanger side, the side rail may run relativily flat or arch a little.<P>If you, like me, end up with the fram that arches about an inch, you will need to modify that sides engine mount (cut it an inch lower) to get the motor so sit level on the frame.<P>Not a major mod at all, just something you may run into.  For me, it was a surprise to get the motor mounted THEN see that it was not level!  Turns out to be no big deal.  Cut-n-paste.<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
